Rotates Administrator's password on DC01 to close out the exposure from earlier in this
exercise (its value had been typed into a Task Scheduler credential store on VM 102). The
account is disabled, so no login is needed with the new value — the goal is only to invalidate
the old one. The new value is never returned in out-data or recorded anywhere, an improvement on
this project's earlier bootstrap-reset pattern, which echoed a throwaway value into out-data and
relied on manual redaction before filing.

Command (first attempt, failed): qm guest exec 100 -- powershell.exe -Command "Set-ADAccountPassword
  -Identity Administrator -Reset -NewPassword (ConvertTo-SecureString (-join ((33..126) |
  Get-Random -Count 24 | %{[char]$_})) -AsPlainText -Force); 'RESET_COMPLETE'"
Host: DC01 (VM 100), via qm guest exec from Proxmox host
Timestamp: 2026-09-01 (UTC, exact time not recorded)

{
   "err-data" : "At line:1 char:142\r\n+ ... (-join ((33..126) | Get-Random -Count 24 | %{[char]Get-ADUser Adminis ...\r\n+                                                        ~~~~~~~~~~\r\nUnexpected token 'Get-ADUser' in expression or statement.\r\n    + CategoryInfo          : ParserError: (:) [], ParentContainsErrorRecordException\r\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : UnexpectedToken\r\n \r\n",
   "exitcode" : 1,
   "exited" : 1
}

Cause: same bash `$_` double-quoting bug already documented in `administrator-bootstrap-reenable.json`
earlier this exercise — the outer `-Command` argument was double-quoted, so bash expanded `$_`
(here, to the last argument of a prior command) before PowerShell ever saw the script. No change
was made to DC01 by this attempt; the account remained Enabled:False, PasswordLastSet unchanged,
confirmed below before retrying.

Command (verify no-op after the failed attempt): qm guest exec 100 -- powershell.exe -Command
  "Get-ADUser Administrator -Properties Enabled,PasswordLastSet | Select Enabled,PasswordLastSet"
Host: DC01 (VM 100), via qm guest exec from Proxmox host
Timestamp: 2026-09-01 (UTC, exact time not recorded)

{
   "exitcode" : 0,
   "exited" : 1,
   "out-data" : "\r\nEnabled PasswordLastSet    \r\n------- ---------------    \r\n  False 9/1/2026 8:01:57 AM\r\n\r\n\r\n"
}

Command (corrected, whole -Command argument single-quoted for bash): qm guest exec 100 --
  powershell.exe -Command 'Set-ADAccountPassword -Identity Administrator -Reset -NewPassword
  (ConvertTo-SecureString (-join ((33..126) | Get-Random -Count 24 | %{[char]$_})) -AsPlainText
  -Force); "RESET_COMPLETE"'
Host: DC01 (VM 100), via qm guest exec from Proxmox host
Timestamp: 2026-09-01 (UTC, exact time not recorded)

{
   "exitcode" : 0,
   "exited" : 1,
   "out-data" : "RESET_COMPLETE\r\n"
}

Command (verify): qm guest exec 100 -- powershell.exe -Command "Get-ADUser Administrator
  -Properties Enabled,PasswordLastSet | Select Enabled,PasswordLastSet"
Host: DC01 (VM 100), via qm guest exec from Proxmox host
Timestamp: 2026-09-01 (UTC, exact time not recorded)

{
   "exitcode" : 0,
   "exited" : 1,
   "out-data" : "\r\nEnabled PasswordLastSet    \r\n------- ---------------    \r\n  False 9/1/2026 1:08:22 PM\r\n\r\n\r\n"
}

RESULT: PasswordLastSet moved from 8:01:57 AM to 1:08:22 PM, confirming the rotation landed.
Enabled remains False. The password typed into VM 102's Task Scheduler on 09-01 is no longer
valid. No password value for this account exists in this repo or was ever printed to this
channel at any point in this rotation.
